3. TOP 5 DEEP DIVES

#1 Jevlike =E2=80=94 TEST NOW

This is the closest concrete open implementation yet found to the JEV
mechanism: context + variable option set =E2=86=92 probability distribution=
,
without prose generation. More interestingly, it extends the same
option-attention head into visual action selection for Doom/chess.
That makes JEV less like a niche API format and more like a candidate
generic fast-control primitive.

Privately experiment: put Jevlike between an LLM planner and QP. Give
it 5-20 bounded actions such as ALLOW / DENY / ESCALATE / SANDBOX /
REQUIRE_PROOF and compare latency, calibration and policy consistency
against an LLM JSON classifier.

Falsifier: no meaningful latency/cost/reliability advantage after
calibration on real Privately decisions.

#2 Native Agent Runtime Router =E2=80=94 ADOPT/COMPARE

NAR is unusually aligned with the existing QP/atask direction:
deterministic model-free kernel, bounded waiting, workspace locking,
verification, one repair, cancellation confirmation, budgets,
recovery, usage accounting and per-agent scoring. This is much closer
to a reusable autonomy kernel than another chat-agent framework.

Experiment: map NAR=E2=80=99s run/wait/inspect/cancel contract against QP
task/proof/budget objects. Identify primitives to copy rather than
integrating wholesale.

#3 Pipelock =E2=80=94 ADOPT/BAKEOFF

Pipelock is moving beyond a generic MCP firewall toward an external
evidence-producing mediator: it scans bidirectional traffic and emits
signed receipts from outside the agent. This directly overlaps
Privately=E2=80=99s thesis that evidence should be produced at the authorit=
y
boundary, not self-reported by the agent.

Experiment: run identical benign exfiltration/rug-pull/tool-chain
scenarios through Pipelock, Veil MCP and QP prototype. Compare
observable evidence, false positives, latency and policy
expressiveness.

#4 Recuris =E2=80=94 BUILD PROBE

Recuris=E2=80=99s key distinction is not merely =E2=80=98agent memory=E2=80=
=99: it decomposes
skill memory, uses structured trajectories to locate failure in a
component, patches only that component, then uses deterministic
held-out validation to decide survival. This is extremely close to the
desired QP processor-evolution model.

Experiment: represent one QP processor=E2=80=99s rules as evolvable memory =
and
require paired held-out proof before promotion.

#5 SkillCloak/SkillDetonate =E2=80=94 CONTENT + LAB

The durable lesson is that install-time appearance is not enough. The
research reports >90% bypass for its packing approach across tested
static scanners, while runtime SkillDetonate tracks materialized
instructions and sensitive-data flows. This reinforces the scanner=E2=80=99=
s
earlier TEMPORAL_TRUST_DRIFT finding from a different direction:
authority should attach to observed behaviour and continuing identity,
not merely the artifact reviewed at install time.

4. AGENT FRAMEWORK / MONID-LIKE FRONTIER

Rank: NAR > Dynamic Discovery MCP > ACP Router > SwarmClaw > seslak
Agent Router > AgentRouter client > Agent Harness > forge18 Agent
Router MCP.

Key pattern: Monid=E2=80=99s neighbourhood is splitting into three layers:

- capability discovery/compression =E2=80=94 Dynamic Discovery MCP;

- worker routing/execution =E2=80=94 ACP Router/NAR;

- policy/economics =E2=80=94 seslak Agent Router.

Privately should sit orthogonally across all three as
authority/evidence mediation rather than build another monolith.

5. JEV / DECISION / SELF-IMPROVEMENT FRONTIER

Rank: Jevlike > OpenJev > Recuris > Meta^n > recursive-improve >
recursive-self-improvement > CS224N RSI.

The important expansion is that JEV should be tracked as a mechanism
family, not a brand: direct option scoring, small policy heads,
learned routers and bounded action models. Self-improvement likewise
splits into prompt/harness evolution, memory evolution and weight
evolution. QP can provide the promotion gate across all three.

6. ATTACKER FRONTIER

AART is the best immediate safe benchmark. RedTeam Agent and kali-claw
show the operator layer becoming increasingly agentic. SkillCloak is
more structurally important: attackers can target the gap between
artifact appearance and runtime materialization. No operational
malicious instructions are included here; all proposed work is
isolated defensive testing.

